      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, I think this is because `noreturn` is C-only (`[[noreturn]]` is C++ equivalent).\n\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/attributes/noreturn\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/c/language/_Noreturn\n\nNot sure if there\u0027s a cleaner way of doing it than this:\n\n```\n#ifdef __cplusplus\n[[noreturn]]\n#else\nnoreturn\n#endif\nvoid panic_assert_fail(const char *msg, const char *func,\n\t\t\t\tconst char *fname, int linenum);\n```\n\nI also recall there being some difference between `gcc` and `clang` on this. See [this code](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/system.h;l\u003d376-380;drc\u003d4f6d8ca42115d3c39cbc6a476414df0be629f51e). It looks like the host tests are being built with `gcc` right now.",
